{
  "ref": "Job 11",
  "heRef": "איוב י״א",
  "isComplex": false,
  "text": [
    "Then Zophar the Naamathite said in reply:",
    "<span class=\"poetry indentAll\">Is a multitude of words unanswerable?</span><br><span class=\"poetry indentAll\">Must a loquacious person be right?</span>",
    "<span class=\"poetry indentAll\">Your prattle may silence people;</span><br><span class=\"poetry indentAll\">You may mock without being rebuked,</span>",
    "<span class=\"poetry indentAll\">And say, “My doctrine is pure,</span><br><span class=\"poetry indentAll\">And I have been innocent in Your sight.”</span>",
    "<span class=\"poetry indentAll\">But would that God might speak,</span><br><span class=\"poetry indentAll\">And talk to you directly.</span>",
    "<span class=\"poetry indentAll\">You would be told the secrets of wisdom,</span><br><span class=\"poetry indentAll\">For there are many sides to sagacity;</span><br><span class=\"poetry indentAll\">And know that God has overlooked for you some of your iniquity.<sup class=\"footnote-marker\">a</sup><i class=\"footnote\"><b>For there are … your iniquity </b>Meaning of Heb. uncertain.</i> </span>",
    "<span class=\"poetry indentAll\">Would you discover the mystery of God?</span><br><span class=\"poetry indentAll\">Would you discover the limit of the Almighty?</span>",
    "<span class=\"poetry indentAll\">Higher than heaven—what can you do?</span><br><span class=\"poetry indentAll\">Deeper than Sheol—what can you know?</span>",
    "<span class=\"poetry indentAll\">Its measure is longer than the earth</span><br><span class=\"poetry indentAll\">And broader than the sea.</span>",
    "<span class=\"poetry indentAll\"><sup class=\"footnote-marker\">b</sup><i class=\"footnote\">Meaning of verse uncertain.</i> Should [God] pass by, or confine,</span><br><span class=\"poetry indentAll\">Or call an assembly, who can put a stop to it?</span>",
    "<span class=\"poetry indentAll\">For [God] is aware of deceitful people,</span><br><span class=\"poetry indentAll\">And when seeing iniquity, discerns it.<sup class=\"footnote-marker\">c</sup><i class=\"footnote\"><b>discerns it </b>Heb. “is it not discerned?”</i> </span>",
    "<span class=\"poetry indentAll\">The hollow person will get understanding,</span><br><span class=\"poetry indentAll\">When a wild ass is born a human.<sup class=\"footnote-marker\">d</sup><i class=\"footnote\"><b>The hollow person … born a human </b>Meaning of Heb. uncertain.</i> </span>",
    "<span class=\"poetry indentAll\">But if you direct your mind,</span><br><span class=\"poetry indentAll\">And spread forth your hands toward [God]—</span>",
    "<span class=\"poetry indentAll\">If there is iniquity with you, remove it,</span><br><span class=\"poetry indentAll\">And do not let injustice reside in your tent—</span>",
    "<span class=\"poetry indentAll\">Then, free of blemish, you will hold your head high,</span><br><span class=\"poetry indentAll\">And, when in straits,<sup class=\"footnote-marker\">e</sup><i class=\"footnote\"><b>when in straits </b>Heb. <i>muṣaq</i>; other Heb. editions <i>muṣṣaq</i>, “you will be firm.”</i> be unafraid.</span>",
    "<span class=\"poetry indentAll\">You will then put your misery out of mind,</span><br><span class=\"poetry indentAll\">Consider it as water that has flowed past.</span>",
    "<span class=\"poetry indentAll\">Life will be brighter than noon;<sup class=\"footnote-marker\">f</sup><i class=\"footnote\"><b>Life will be brighter than noon </b>Meaning of Heb. uncertain.</i> </span><br><span class=\"poetry indentAll\">You will shine, you will be like the morning.</span>",
    "<span class=\"poetry indentAll\">You will be secure, for there is hope,</span><br><span class=\"poetry indentAll\">And, entrenched,<sup class=\"footnote-marker\">g</sup><i class=\"footnote\"><b>And, entrenched </b>Meaning of Heb. uncertain.</i> you will rest secure;</span>",
    "<span class=\"poetry indentAll\">You will lie down undisturbed;</span><br><span class=\"poetry indentAll\">The great will court your favor.</span>",
    "<span class=\"poetry indentAll\">But the eyes of the wicked pine away;</span><br><span class=\"poetry indentAll\">Escape is cut off from them;</span><br><span class=\"poetry indentAll\">They have only their last breath to look forward to.</span>"
  ],
